│     I fixed `serialize_sequence_value` in `fastapi/_compat/v2.py` so optional sequences work with both `Optional[...]` and PEP 604 `X | │
│ None` annotations, and submitted the patch (1 file, 1661 bytes).                                                                        │
│                                                                                                                                         │
│     The function only recognised `typing.Union`, so `list[int] | None` (`types.UnionType`) fell through to the sequence assertion. It   │
│ also always took the first non-None union member, even when that member wasn't a sequence. It now accepts both union forms and picks    │
│ the first non-None member that is a sequence type.                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                         │
│     A quick manual check with `list[int] | None` and `Optional[Sequence[str]]` query parameters returned the expected lists and `None`  │
│ when absent. The pytest run selected no tests, so the existing suite was not exercised.                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                         │
│     I did not adopt `typing-inspection`, since the local `lenient_issubclass` check covers this case without a new dependency.          │
